; a mass released from height in a gravitational field.
; gravity (F=mg) acts downward continuously — svayambhu-siddha.
; janya (what it needs): mass, height, gravity.
; phala (what follows): velocity at impact = √(2gh), KE = mgh.
; then: collision with surface → coefficient-of-restitution determines bounce.
; 
; the tantra (falling-step.tantra2) implements the step:
; given [object, height, h] and g → emit [object, velocity, √(2gh)]
; given [object, velocity, v] and surface e → emit [object, velocity-after, e*v]
; iterate until velocity below threshold → object at rest.

(kosha falling
  (vishesa common-sense-varga processes-varga)
  (swarupa tinanta bhave-prayoga)
  (janya gravity height mass)
  (phala velocity kinetic-energy collision-varga)
  (abheda free-fall)
  (yukta potential-energy kinetic-energy coefficient-of-restitution normal-force))
